{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 One of them decided to speak so that the world would know the aberrations that were committed to subdue the Uighurs in that remote region of the country. Qelbinur Sidik taught children at a school there. One day, without much explanation, she was forging the force to teach Mandarin to the detainees for three months. You'll never forget that traumatic experience. Learning the language is one of the conditions that the regional authorities impose on those who settle there.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 He began his obligatory work in March 2017. She went from caring for children between the age of six and thirteen to older adults. When he first saw them, he couldn't believe it: they were all chained, feet and hands, as if they were high-danger criminals. Sidik, a Uzbek who had lived there for almost 30 years, did not quite understand why if those she had in front of her were like her, migrants in search of a better life they did not find.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The teacher recounted some of the horror. "When the guards drank at night, the cops told each other how they raped and tortured the girls," she said. Sidik saw with his own eyes how a woman died as a result of these group rapes. In a herd. "There was no spark of life on his face. His cheeks were colorless, he wasn't breathing," he recalled. The victim was carried by other guards and a policewoman confirmed to her what had happened: torture, rape and the consequent murder.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The transformation of the detainees was evident over the days. Those "students in the process of re-education" who first arrived at the center where she worked looked healthy, in good physical condition and well fed. However, within a few days, it was all skin and bones. On many occasions, when he turned around to write on the board, he listened to many of those present cry in shame. He also heard other sounds, more guttural and strange, coming from other rooms in the building. There were no classes there, just torture.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
